R"VG(
# modern7.vg (H-04, the second pass): the lyrics of a song on a disc. A verse is a couplet: a scene of that people's town (its trams and
# quarters, its feasts, its food sold from carts, its river, its crafts) and an image to answer it, each line made of parts; the chorus is
# the song's own and comes back (`keep`), each people with its own few (`people=5`): one people sings of its river, another of its
# sacred colour, a third of its trams.

genre.lyrics (words=30..90)
  {ly.verse}\n{ly.chorus}\n{ly.verse}\n{ly.chorus}
  {ly.verse}\n{ly.chorus}\n{ly.bridge}\n{ly.chorus}
  {ly.verse}\n{ly.verse}\n{ly.chorus}
  {ly.verse}\n{ly.chorus}\n{ly.verse}\n{ly.bridge}\n{ly.chorus}

ly.verse
  (4) {ly.a}\n{ly.b}
  (once stage>=1) They say the water's going, they say a lot of things,\nI say hold on to me, {ly.hold},
  (once stage>=1) They're closing the line to the outer towns,\nand your {ly.kin} is still out there with the {herd},

# ---- the scene ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

ly.a (share=0.6)
  I met you {ly.where} {ly.when},
  We grew up {ly.grew},
  There's a {msg.transit} out of {$home} {ly.every},
  My {ly.kin} said the {crop} was {ly.better} then,
  You wore your {colour.any} {garment.n} to {feast.custom},
  The {bird} came back to the {ly.roofs} of {$home},
  Your {ly.kin} sold {food} from a {ly.cart} on {streets.of},
  We used to {ly.swim} in {river} when the {ly.summers} were long,
  I learned the {craft} from my {ly.kin}'s hands,
  We danced till the {fuel} ran out {ly.inwhere},
  They shut the {craft} works on a morning in {season.now},
  I keep your old {vessel.one.n} on the {ly.shelf},
  Down where {river} runs under the {ly.road},
  We sat on the steps of {holyplace} {ly.howlong},
  You left your {garment.n} on the {msg.transit} {ly.when},
  We drank {drink} on the roof {ly.when},
  My {ly.kin} kept {herd} on the hill above {$home},
  The {craft} works whistle blew at {ly.hour},
  You came back from {$seat} with {ly.brought},
  We stood in the queue for {food} {ly.when},
  They painted the doors {colour.any} {ly.when},
  I counted the {bird} on the wires {ly.when},
  You played {instrument} at {feast.custom},
  The rain came down on {streets.of} {ly.when},
  We hid from {weather} in {ly.hide},
  (has:$home.quarter) They're playing {instrument} down in {$home.quarter},
  (has:$home.landmark) There's a light still on in {$home.landmark},
  (has:$home.landmark) I wrote your name in {colour.any} paint by {$home.landmark},
  (inv.radio=1) The radio's playing the {festival} songs {ly.again},
