# ---- the answer ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

ly.b (share=0.6)
  you were laughing at something {ly.someone} didn't {ly.see},
  the {fruit} were ripe and so were we,
  and the {bird} were singing like they {ly.knew},
  I can still smell the {food} on the {ly.stairs},
  and {instrument} was always out of tune,
  you said {proverb}, and I {ly.laughed},
  and I never told you, and I never {ly.will},
  the lamps were {colour.any} and so was {ly.sky},
  and nobody came to tell us to go {ly.home},
  and the {ly.wx} came in like it owned the {ly.place},
  I still have the {ly.kept} and the {garment.n},
  and the {ly.olds} shook their heads at {ly.us},
  we had nothing, and we had {ly.all},
  you swore {oath} that you'd {ly.stay},
  you were going {ly.otherway}, {ly.always},
  and the {msg.transit} went by {ly.full},
  and your {ly.kin} said {ly.said},
  and the {crop} grew tall where the old {ly.oldthing} stood,
  and I swore {oath} I'd {ly.swore} by {festival},
  and the whole of {streets.of} heard,
  and {skyone} looked down and {ly.looked},
  and the {herd} came home without us,
  we were young and the {drink} was cheap,
  and the smoke of the {craft} works was {ly.smoke},
  and I learned your name from the {ly.learnt},
  (inv.radio=1) you had the radio on and the window {ly.down},
